{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_whole_house_system", "label": "Whole House System", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "White point-of-entry cabinet with copper riser and ball valve, placed on the front wall where the mains comes in from the street meter."}, {"id": "readme_under_sink_system", "label": "Under Sink System", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three-canister RO unit plus pressure tank and a dedicated tap, placed inside the kitchen sink cabinet."}, {"id": "readme_rainwater_system", "label": "Rainwater System", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stainless three-canister unit with UV lamp and gauges on top, placed on the right gable wall beside the rainwater tank."}, {"id": "readme_x_ray_reveal", "label": "X-Ray Reveal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selecting a system makes the unit's cover, cartridge housings and the pipework the route runs inside go see-through so the water is visible for the whole journey rather than only where it crosses open ground."}, {"id": "readme_cutaway", "label": "Roof and Front Wall Cutaway", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The under-sink view fades the roof and front wall away so the camera can get into the kitchen; Reset view puts everything back."}, {"id": "readme_route_legs", "label": "Route Legs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each system's route is authored as a chain of legs (one pipe run each) tagged with stage, whether it passes through a filter element, pace, and whether it is buried. Every leg boundary is a real control point of the curve, so each stage's span along the path is measured rather than guessed."}, {"id": "readme_stage_badges", "label": "Stage Badges", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A numbered badge hangs at each of the four stages, anchored to the middle of that stage's element; the selected one takes the accent colour and grows. Past a few metres the unselected badges fade so the wide view carries one 'you are here' pin rather than four overlapping discs."}, {"id": "readme_hard_edge_outline", "label": "Hard-Edge Outline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The active unit is outlined with its own hard edges in the accent colour rather than an inverted hull. The hull was tried first but depends on the object writing depth, and these units stop writing depth once the x-ray fades their covers; stencil masking still left a wide fringe. Edges sit exactly on the surface so they behave the same whether the cover is solid or see-through. Drawn via drei's Line, not lineSegments, because WebGL clamps native line width to one pixel."}, {"id": "readme_colour_ramp_across_element", "label": "Colour Ramp Across Element", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The water colour ramp sits across each filter element so a bubble visibly clears while it is working through the cartridge instead of changing colour once it is already out the far side."}, {"id": "readme_time_spaced_bubble_column", "label": "Time-Spaced Bubble Column", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bubbles are spaced evenly in time rather than distance so they crowd through media and the pressure tank and spread out in open pipe, and can never overtake one another. Each rides at its own offset from the centreline and turns slowly around it so the column churns, and stretches along its travel direction in proportion to speed. Every system takes the same ten seconds end to end regardless of how much of the route is slow."}, {"id": "readme_grit_capture", "label": "Grit Capture", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Specks riding in with the raw water are each given a point on the face of the first element to stop at, biased toward the leading edge, and sit there a moment before fading."}, {"id": "readme_route_line", "label": "Route Line", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A thin line traces the whole path carrying the same gradient, faint where the run is buried and lit along the selected stage. It is thinner than the narrowest pipe it runs inside, so it shows only in the gaps: buried runs and inside the cartridges."}, {"id": "readme_walkthrough_timeline", "label": "Walkthrough as a Timeline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The play button runs a looping guided tour of the four stages, 3.2 seconds each. It is a timeline rather than a timer: one playhead in seconds, and the stage showing is whichever dwell the playhead is inside. That is what makes Play, Pause and Resume honest. Play starts at the stage on screen and flies the camera straight in instead of waiting at the wide view for the first stage change."}, {"id": "readme_pause_freeze_frame", "label": "Pause as Freeze-Frame", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pause stops the playhead and the water together (bubbles held mid-cartridge, grit held on the element face) while the camera stays free, so a paused tour can be orbited and inspected. UI motion that is not simulation (fly-to in flight, route highlight sliding on, badges tinting) still settles."}, {"id": "readme_resume_from_same_instant", "label": "Resume Honours Remaining Dwell", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resume carries on from the same instant for both the tour and the water; the remainder of the current stage is honoured rather than restarted."}, {"id": "readme_scrubbable_progress_bar", "label": "Scrubbable Progress Bar", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The progress bar is the playhead: click or drag anywhere and the tour goes there, landing on the stage that point falls in. Its colours are the water's own per-stage list, raw at the left and finished at the right, so the bar is the journey in miniature with a hairline at each stage boundary."}, {"id": "readme_stage_seek", "label": "Stage Seek Keeps Tour State", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Picking a stage from the dots, keyboard or scene seeks: the tour moves there and keeps whatever state it had, so a paused tour can be stepped stage by stage with the water held at each. Switching system or resetting the view ends the tour."}, {"id": "readme_keyboard_controls", "label": "Keyboard Tour Controls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Space plays and pauses; the arrow keys step between stages; Home and End go to the first and last stage."}, {"id": "readme_ui_chrome_over_canvas", "label": "UI Chrome Over Canvas", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The UI chrome is plain React and CSS layered over the canvas; none of it is drawn inside Three.js."}, {"id": "readme_light_theme_accent_switch", "label": "Light Theme Accent Switch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "styles/index.css is a light theme whose accent colour is switched by the data-system attribute on .app; picking a system switches the UI accent."}, {"id": "readme_base_colour_surfaces", "label": "Base Colour Surfaces", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Surfaces are base colours only. Timber (deck, floor, window frames) is the obvious candidate for textures later; the cladding could take a vertical-board normal map."}, {"id": "readme_hand_written_orbit_rig", "label": "Hand-Written Orbit Rig", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The camera is a custom rig (useOrbitRig), not drei's OrbitControls: the click-vs-drag threshold and the fly-to tween with angle normalisation (so it never unwinds laps of auto-rotate) are load-bearing for the interaction."}, {"id": "readme_fadegroup_needsupdate", "label": "FadeGroup needsUpdate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "FadeGroup flips material.transparent at runtime; three bakes that flag into the compiled shader, so it sets needsUpdate when the flag changes. Without it a material that started opaque stays opaque regardless of opacity."}, {"id": "readme_fill_rate_budget", "label": "Fill-Rate Budget", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The scene is fill-rate bound, not geometry bound: halving resolution roughly doubles frame rate. So dpr is capped at 1.5 rather than 2 and the rim light does not cast shadows; on integrated graphics at 1600x1000 the pair take a high-DPI display from about 12fps to about 24. Smooth motion matters more because water that stutters stops reading as water. Measure before re-enabling either."}, {"id": "readme_frame_rate_independent_damping", "label": "Frame-Rate Independent Damping", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Anything animated per frame damps with Math.min(1, delta * rate), never a fixed per-frame fraction; otherwise transitions run at different speeds on different monitors and look broken rather than slow on a slow machine. Transitions cap delta at 0.05."}, {"id": "readme_real_time_clocks_with_stall_cap", "label": "Real-Time Clocks with Stall Cap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The walkthrough's clock and the water's clock are the exception to damping: they must keep real time, so they take the frame's whole delta capped at a quarter second rather than 0.05. The cap only swallows a stall (background tab, shader compile); a machine merely struggling still gets a tour that runs to time and water at the right speed. Both clocks read a paused flag rather than being torn down, so resuming is just letting the delta count again."}, {"id": "readme_water_clock_negative_priority", "label": "Water Clock at useFrame Priority -1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The water's clock is stepped in a useFrame at priority -1 so it is ahead of the bubbles and grit that read it in the same frame. r3f runs frame callbacks in priority order; only a priority above zero switches off automatic render, so a negative priority is safe purely for ordering."}, {"id": "readme_playhead_written_to_dom", "label": "Playhead Written Straight to DOM", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The play bar's playhead is written directly to the DOM as a CSS variable that both the fill and the knob read, from a subscription on the walkthrough. Holding it in React state would re-render the app, canvas included, every frame."}, {"id": "readme_adding_a_product_checklist", "label": "Adding a Product Checklist", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adding a product: a mount point in layout.js, a view / stages / legs entry in systems.js, copy in data/constants.js, a component under three/products/, and render it in Scene.jsx with unitProps(key)."}, {"id": "readme_media_leg_declaration", "label": "Single media Leg Declaration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Write legs in flow order, each listing only the points it adds. Marking the run through each filter element media: true with a slow pace is the one declaration that places the colour change, the stage marker and the slowdown. buried: true draws the route line faintly where a run disappears underground or under the floor."}, {"id": "readme_revealed_pipework_thinning", "label": "Revealed Pipework Thinning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A product whose route runs inside modelled pipework should thin that pipework out on revealed, as the three existing units do; otherwise the water is hidden inside its own plumbing for most of the journey."}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_whole_house_system", "target": "src_three_products_wholehouseunit_wholehouseunit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_under_sink_system", "target": "src_three_products_undersinkunit_undersinkunit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_rainwater_system", "target": "src_three_products_rainwaterunit_rainwaterunit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_under_sink_system", "target": "readme_cutaway", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_x_ray_reveal", "target": "src_three_parts_fadegroup_fadegroup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_x_ray_reveal", "target": "src_three_parts_canister_canister", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_x_ray_reveal", "target": "readme_hard_edge_outline", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_x_ray_reveal", "target": "readme_revealed_pipework_thinning", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_cutaway", "target": "src_three_parts_fadegroup_fadegroup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_cutaway", "target": "src_three_house_house", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_route_legs", "target": "src_three_systems_systems", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_route_legs", "target": "src_three_path_buildpath", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_route_legs", "target": "readme_stage_badges", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "READM